                <pb facs="0316" n="304" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg304"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.91/101a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargè in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ford</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-13T23:00:00-04:00">January 13,
                            1944—11 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>23. The Department proposes to raise the Legation in Tehran to the rank of
                    Embassy. Please inform the Iranian Government and inquire whether this step
                    meets with its approval and whether it agrees similarly to raise the status of
                    the Iranian Legation in Washington.</p>
                <p>For your information only: The British have been advised informally of the
                    Department’s intended action.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
